- Story & Context: Legend holds this track was recovered from an unspooled reel recorder left inside a sealed compressor room after the 2021 cave-in at Samcheok Tunnel Seven, where the air blowers kept rattling long after the crew stopped answering. The groove layers airy, 1950s baritone saxophone counterpoint over an impossibly rapid, mechanical hi-hat stutter that mimics four hundred pipe-strikes a minute, culminating in the ghostly, pitch-bent vocal cry: "The mountain can crush our ribs, but it drinks our melody." Today in Seoul's subterranean after-hours clubs, dancers ceremonially crush blown-glass ornaments under their boots whenever the vicious hi-hat breakdown drops.
